body:
@spinalcord thank you for sharing, intuitively all of the changes you mention make sense and seem like what the solution for this should be.

When testing in my game, while the first exit out of that nested state does avoid the T pose and prints `SM DEBUG: Freezing 'moving' at End to prevent T-Pose.`, every alternate entry into that state only shows the T pose, printing nothing.

https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/730c5d44-539a-4003-841d-028e324e6328

@vaner-org Using the ghost frame attempt: You can change `nested` to `root` on the suspect state machine that’s causing the alternating T-pose. At least, that’s how I reproduced/solved what I saw in your video (i think). I’m not sure what the best strategy is overall, you could maybe swap the attempt in the godot src so it works with `State Machine Type: nested` and not with `State Machine Type: Root` or same boilerplate on both. 

